From d8b39612750d937df98983553877452c92b9d838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saurabh Davala <saurabh.davala@docker.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Oct 2025 17:34:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Skip security checks for container environments (compose
 networking)

Add DOCKER_MCP_IN_CONTAINER=1 check to both security middleware to support
Docker Compose networking where services connect using container hostnames.

Changes:
- authenticationMiddleware: Skip auth when DOCKER_MCP_IN_CONTAINER=1
- originSecurityHandler: Skip origin validation when DOCKER_MCP_IN_CONTAINER=1
- Added tests for both container mode scenarios

Why this is safe:
- Container networks are isolated (not exposed to internet)
- No web browsers in container environments (no DNS rebinding possible)
- Services connect using container hostnames (e.g., http://gateway:8080)
- Different threat model than local development

Both middleware now consistently check the env var for compose compatibility.
---
 pkg/gateway/auth.go           |  7 +++++++
 pkg/gateway/auth_test.go      | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/gateway/transport.go      | 11 +++++++++++
 pkg/gateway/transport_test.go | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 76 insertions(+)

