From 3150f8284b023f2f4e030c82e1f14f1c4776deb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saurabh Davala <saurabh.davala@docker.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Oct 2025 08:00:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Address security researcher feedback on Origin validation

Implements all feedback from JLLeitschuh's PR review:

1. CRITICAL: Remove container check from Origin validation
   - Origin validation now ALWAYS runs (even when DOCKER_MCP_IN_CONTAINER=1)
   - Safe because container services don't send Origin headers
   - Protects against exposed container ports (e.g., -p 8080:8080)
   - Auth middleware still skips for containers (trusted network)

2. Add IPv6 localhost support
   - Allow ::1 (IPv6 loopback) in isAllowedOrigin()
   - Added 4 IPv6 test cases

3. Improve error messages for debugging
   - Error now shows: "Origin must be localhost, 127.0.0.1, or ::1, got: <actual>"
   - Helps developers debug Origin issues quickly

4. Fix test comment accuracy
   - Updated 0.0.0.0 test comments to reference RFC 1122
   - Fixed DNS rebinding test to clarify actual attack (evil.com resolves to 0.0.0.0)
   - Removed container mode test (no longer applicable)

All tests pass (26 isAllowedOrigin + 5 originSecurityHandler + 5 auth + 5 combined).

Defense-in-depth:
- Auth middleware: Skips for DOCKER_MCP_IN_CONTAINER (compose trust)
- Origin validation: Always validates (protects exposed ports)
